It would be fun to create a two-player version of Nethack! You could
play with your buddy online.

Here's the way it could work:

When there is no combat situation, i.e. no monster is within view,
there are no "turns" and you can freely move around and do whatever
you want without having to wait for your partner to make his move.

As soon as a monster appears, then it switches to turn-based, where
you can think and plan your moves one at a time.

I think something like this could work.

I'm not sure how ESP would be handled. For example, would it switch to
turn-based as soon as an ESPed monster in another room is detected? Or
maybe not. Maybe these monsters would just have a default movement for
every average 1 move between the 2 player characters, i.e. if one
character moves twice or if they each move once, then the monsters all
get one turn.

